From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:34:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: Verify the fallback
 written on an IRQ storm

When the PMU's source events storm, the fallback limit was written
without checking the write or reading it back, and recorded as the
current limit either way. Write it through tristar_set_code(), which
verifies the read-back and records only a limit that took, and say when
the limit is unverified. This applies to every board with the Tristar
charger (A7, A8X, A9 and A10 iPads).

[Orchard: from OrchardLinux/orchard#205 (tompta1, 09038adf),
 kernel/patches/drivers/power/0052, ported to the charger without the
 D2355 chip operations.]

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index 1917f0978..3c0c29bd0 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -1309,7 +1309,6 @@ static bool tristar_event_debounce(struct tristar_charger *chg)
  */
 static void tristar_source_event(struct tristar_charger *chg)
 {
-	u32 reg = chg->limit_reg;
 	unsigned int i;
 	u64 now;
 
@@ -1331,10 +1330,11 @@ static void tristar_source_event(struct tristar_charger *chg)
 		chg->storm_count = 0;
 	}
 	if (++chg->storm_count > TRISTAR_IRQ_STORM) {
-		dev_crit(chg->dev, "PMU source events storming; holding the fallback\n");
-		regmap_write(chg->regmap, reg, TRISTAR_CHG_FALLBACK_CODE);
-		WRITE_ONCE(chg->code, TRISTAR_CHG_FALLBACK_CODE);
 		WRITE_ONCE(chg->phase, TRISTAR_FAULT);
+		if (tristar_set_code(chg, TRISTAR_CHG_FALLBACK_CODE))
+			dev_crit(chg->dev, "PMU source events storming; input limit unverified\n");
+		else
+			dev_crit(chg->dev, "PMU source events storming; holding the fallback\n");
 		for (i = TRISTAR_IRQ_SOURCE; i < chg->nirqs; i++)
 			disable_irq_nosync(chg->irqs[i]);
 	}
